DevOps Interview Command Series — Networking (Day 2) 🌐

Networking is non-negotiable in DevOps.
Whether it’s Kubernetes services, load balancers, cloud VPCs, firewalls, or debugging outages — strong networking skills decide production stability.

If you’re preparing for DevOps / SRE / Cloud interviews, these are the Networking commands you must know:

“ip a
ip r
ip link
ifconfig
route -n

ss -tulnp
netstat -tulnp
lsof -i :PORT

ping host
traceroute host
mtr host

curl URL
curl -I URL
wget URL

nslookup domain
dig domain
host domain

tcpdump -i eth0
tcpdump -nn port 80

nmcli dev status
ethtool eth0”

🎯 Interview Focus
• Debug connectivity issues
• Identify which service is listening on which port
• Troubleshoot DNS resolution
• Analyze packet-level traffic
• Validate network routes & gateways


